{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The follower handler keeps `Success=false` until the synchronous `StoreLogs` call returns successfully, and returns immediately on a storage error. The network handler then encodes that RPC’s response through its own reply channel. This explains why the truncation result alone does not establish false storage support. Crash durability and retained-log consistency remain separate gaps."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nsources=[\n {'id':'follower-append-full','file':'raft.go','start_line':1440,'end_line':1580,'kind':'code_observation'},\n {'id':'network-command-association','file':'net_transport.go','start_line':603,'end_line':687,'kind':'code_observation'},\n {'id':'network-command-response','file':'net_transport.go','start_line':720,'end_line':767,'kind':'code_observation'},\n {'id':'inmem-store-write','file':'inmem_store.go','start_line':60,'end_line':79,'kind':'code_observation'},\n {'id':'log-store-contract','file':'log.go','start_line':110,'end_line':142,'kind':'interface_statement'}]\nq={\n 'disposition':'explained_by_existing_mechanism','preferred_check':'source_review',\n 'question':'For a normal non-heartbeat AppendEntries request containing a newly appended suffix, can the actual follower handler publish Success=true while its StoreLogs call is still pending or after that call returns an error, supplying the successful response prefix used in the network truncation check? The discriminator is the order of the actual StoreLogs return, Success assignment and per-request response publication.',\n 'importance':'The checked local network consumer promotes match after a decode failure when partial fields contain Success=true. Whether that implies false stored-prefix support depends on the actual producer. An acknowledgement emitted before or despite failed storage would make a stronger concern possible; this question addresses that producer order only.',\n 'source_ids':[s['id'] for s in sources],\n 'participants':['Follower main RPC handler','Selected LogStore implementation','NetworkTransport per-connection handler','Leader network-response consumer considered only as downstream context'],\n 'objects':['One nonempty AppendEntries request with a new suffix','Fresh AppendEntriesResponse initialized with Success=false','Synchronous StoreLogs call for newEntries','RPC-specific respCh'],\n 'contexts':['A1 success establishment depends on A6 storage-call completion','Ordinary non-heartbeat new-entry branch','No duplicate-only append, process crash, store corruption or competing log mutation in this narrow source question','Transport delay or stream truncation affects reply delivery after publication, not handler statement order'],\n 'event_paths':[\n  'appendEntries allocates a fresh response with Success=false and defers rpc.Respond of that same response (raft.go:1440-1453).',\n  'After term and previous-log checks, the handler identifies a new suffix, calls StoreLogs synchronously, and returns immediately on a non-nil error (raft.go:1504-1544).',\n  'After successful storage return and configuration processing, the handler updates last-log metadata. Success=true is assigned only near the end of the handler (raft.go:1546-1579).',\n  'The deferred reply therefore cannot precede return from the synchronous storage call. In the storage-error branch it publishes Success=false.',\n  'NetworkTransport allocates a fresh respCh per command, classifies nonempty Entries as non-heartbeat, dispatches that RPC and encodes the response received on its own respCh. handleConn processes and flushes that response before the next command (net_transport.go:603-687,720-767).'\n ],\n 'activity_classes':['A1','A6'],'behavior_ids':[],'fact_ids':[],'obligation_relation_kind':'establishment',\n 'counterevidence':[\n  'Synchronous storage completion and the storage-error early return protect this particular success producer, despite the separately checked downstream decode-error acceptance discrepancy.',\n  'The network handler pairs each request with a fresh response channel and processes commands serially on its connection; the source does not substitute another request\\\\'s response at this handoff.',\n  'The network check encoded a scripted genuinely successful full response before truncating it. A partial true success field from that input need not be false information about storage.'\n ],\n 'unknowns':[\n  'This is source review of storage-call ordering, not execution of the actual follower branch and not formal property Evidence.',\n  'A StoreLogs nil return is not independent evidence of crash durability. The deployment-selected store is unknown; built-in InmemStore writes memory and is not a persistent-store guarantee. Built-in and external store contracts remain distinct.',\n  'Duplicate-only requests, existing-prefix correctness, stale last-log metadata after failed deletion/write sequences, snapshot restore, subsequent log invalidation and restart histories are excluded and unresolved.',\n  'Request/response association is source-grounded here; no full elected-leader-to-follower history or network implementation calibration was executed by this disposition.',\n  'The checked local findings remain: failed-future Response access and network decode-error match promotion. This producer protection neither repairs nor retracts either interface-level finding.',\n  'No false quorum, unsafe committed entry, application discrepancy or client-visible consequence has been established. A stronger claim needs an actual same-history false-support producer or invalidation relation and its downstream consequence.'\n ],\n 'priority':2,\n 'trigger_rationale':'Review of network check d06a50c84a414f0fbe4d3e5fd85b6496 identified actual follower success production as the next causal gap. Reading that producer finds storage-before-success and per-request publication rather than evidence of an early or error-success acknowledgement. Decode failure must not be conflated with StoreLogs failure.'\n}\ns={'action':'explained','parent_candidate_id':'616eb4879de0480f805161902cfd632b','sources':sources,'question':q,\n 'rationale':'Scoped producer-order suspicion is explained by existing synchronous storage-before-success and error-return mechanisms. This is a distinct successor question linked to the checked network-consumption candidate, not a semantic revision of either accepted obligation. Source observations establish that a newly appended suffix cannot produce Success=true through this handler before StoreLogs returns or when StoreLogs returns an error. They do not establish actual durable data, a complete legal replication history, or general consensus safety. The measured downstream discrepancies remain unchanged.',\n 'counterevidence_resolution':'No prior counterevidence or measured result is removed. The independent storage-call ordering mechanism limits the broader inference from the scripted-success truncation fixture; store durability and other history paths remain explicit unknowns.',\n 'resume_conditions':[],'obligation':None,'bindings':[]}\nPath('submission.json').write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nimport jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(s,json.load(open('../native-submission.schema.json')))\nprint('Scoped producer explanation schema validated.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
